Well, your main problem is that you're playing the graphical version of
NetHack, and thus have no idea what letters are what monsters, and, more
importantly, what symbols are what item classes.

To know this, refer to the Guidebook, chapter 3.3. For example, a scroll
is a "?", while a potion is a "!".

So, if you want to pick up all potions and scrolls you encounter, you need
to have two lines in your defaults.nh file:

OPTIONS=autopickup
OPTIONS=pickup_types:!?

Or one line:

OPTIONS=autopickup,pickup_types:?!

Most other options may be set in a similar way. They always consist of
either one word (like autopickup) which may be negated by putting "no" or
"!" in front of it (noautopickup or !autopickup), or they are compound
options (like pickup_types), consisting of a word, followed by a colon
(":"), followed by a value.

My options file as an example (all comments "#" have been deleted for
clarity):

OPTIONS=IBMGraphics
OPTIONS=altkeyhandler:nh340key.dll
OPTIONS=name:Kroisos,role:healer,race:gnome,gender:male,align:random
OPTIONS=dogname:Rothond,catname:Snertkat,fruit:mandarijntje
OPTIONS=horsename:Kolerebeest
OPTIONS=autopickup,pickup_types:$"=/!?+(*%[
OPTIONS=autodig,autoquiver,pushweapon
OPTIONS=packorder:)["=(%!?/+*0_`
OPTIONS=scores:10 top/2 around/own
OPTIONS=nolegacy,verbose,nonews
OPTIONS=menustyle:combination
OPTIONS=msg_window:combination
OPTIONS=msghistory:100,boulder:0
OPTIONS=time,showexp,number_pad:2,lit_corridor
OPTIONS=disclose:+i +a +v +g +c
OPTIONS=suppress_alert:3.3.1
OPTIONS=!rest_on_space
OPTIONS=hilite_pet,toptenwin
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*chest*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*box*"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*grey stone"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*gray stone"
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION=">*loadstone"
